issue.body:
A required `MutuallyExclusiveFlags` group on a parent command is enforced before the subcommand parses the flag, so the same command line fails or succeeds depending on where the flag sits relative to the subcommand name.

```go
cmd := &cli.Command{
    Name: "root",
    MutuallyExclusiveFlags: []cli.MutuallyExclusiveFlags{{
        Required: true,
        Flags:    [][]cli.Flag{{&cli.StringFlag{Name: "alpha"}}},
    }},
    Commands: []*cli.Command{{
        Name:   "sub",
        Action: func(context.Context, *cli.Command) error { return nil },
    }},
}

cmd.Run(ctx, []string{"root", "sub", "--alpha", "hello"}) // error: one of these flags needs to be provided: alpha
cmd.Run(ctx, []string{"root", "--alpha", "hello", "sub"}) // ok
```

Group flags are persistent by default and v3 accepts flags after the subcommand name; the same group with `Required: false` works after the name, and a plain `Required: true` flag is validated on the leaf after parsing. Only this group is checked early, because `command_run.go` walks the parent chain for `MutuallyExclusiveFlags` before it resolves and dispatches to the subcommand (the reason the parent-chain walk exists is that the subcommand inherits those flags, which it has not parsed yet at that point).

Expected: `Required` only adds the presence check; the group is validated by the command that actually runs, after it has parsed the inherited flags. `root sub` (flag absent) must still fail with the same message.

